      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1132753496">
          <groundspeak:date>2022-10-19T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP657 Canadian Forces Snowbirds [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I happened to find the nearby traditional in 2019 within my first 4 months of caching (when I had no knowledge of cap logging), and I finally got back today for it. Good thing I had CanadianRockies’ 2015 log to show me the way, because the current GZ is a thistly, grassy mess. Thanks for another cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="1035273373">
          <groundspeak:date>2021-07-21T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1151545">Ringrat</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP657 - Canadian Forces Snowbirds [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I have no idea why I've never stopped to find this cap on the way past before, but I did today and located the cap in short order. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="711428875">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-08-12T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="181446">DanOCan</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP657:  Canadian Forces Snowbirds&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Was passing by picking off some Traditional caches with Tucker the Dog on our way to Lethbridge.  Decided I wouldn't mind finding some Brass Caps along the way too; they may not count as Finds anymore but I still enjoy finding them. [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="703173136">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-07-19T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1685537">nosweat6060</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP657 Canadian Forces Snowbird [FOUND]

This was a nice 2 for 1 stop. The hint was helpful as there was an attractive depression right at the base of the marker post. These Caps can be a challenge in the deep grass. Thanks for keeping this activity alive.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684904222">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-08T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="553001">Bearberrys Cub</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP657 Canadian Forces Snowbirds

N 50° 34.337 W 113° 48.798&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After finding the new Calgary brass cap, I headed south to look for a few caches that while not new, were new since 2014.  Temperatures were great and the sun was shining so what better thing to do than geocache.  Quick find.  OFTH has been emailed with the information.  TFTBC&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
